projects.description:
Building on previous discussions held with national authorities, particularly during the second GCM Implementation Sub-Committee meeting (see above), the projects aims to contribute to efforts by the Government of Sri Lanka towards data-driven, evidence-based policy-making for migration management, in view of the country’s commitment to global frameworks such as the GCM and the 2030 Agenda.

Outcome: Relevant government stakeholders, as identified by the GCM Implementation Sub-Committee, institutionalise a robust mechanism for the collection and dissemination of migration-related data, to promote and sustain gender-sensitive, evidence-based practice for the implementation of the GCM and the 2030 Agenda.

Output 1.1: A national Data Task Force is established and operationalized; 

Output 1.2: Recommendations on enhancing sustainable, gender-sensitive migration-related data processes are drafted and validated by the national Data Task Force, based on the findings of a comprehensive mapping exercise;       

Output 1.3: Government and other relevant stakeholders have access to structured, gender sensitive migration-related data through a fully operational National Migration Data Portal (NMDP);

Output 1.4: Identified government officials working in the field of migration have the necessary skills and knowledge to sustainably manage the NMDP and sustainably capitalize on its functionalities and added value
